From 217ca87f276108a5c9a63ccadd13c178527f234f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kishor Datta Gupta <2458509+kishordgupta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:02:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add JEPA detector for tabular data (experimental)

JEPA scores a row by how badly the latent representation of its hidden
features can be predicted from the visible ones (Joint-Embedding
Predictive Architecture). Each feature, or group of consecutive
features, is a token; a Transformer encoder embeds the visible tokens
and a light predictor forecasts the embeddings of the hidden ones.
Representation collapse is prevented with SIGReg (LeJEPA), with an EMA
target encoder as an alternative.

- pyod/models/jepa.py: JEPA, on BaseDeepLearningDetector. Scores:
  latent prediction error ('pred'), per-token Mahalanobis distance of
  the embeddings ('embed'), or both ('combined', default).
- pyod/models/_jepa_utils.py: shared network, masking and SIGReg code.
- pyod/test/test_jepa.py: 27 tests; listed in conftest.py with the
  other torch-dependent modules.
- examples/jepa_example.py.
- Docs: API reference entry, model table rows in README.rst and
  docs/index.rst, three bibliography entries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
